# Practical No. 5(A)

## Aim
To manage local component state in React using the `useState` hook.

## Code

### `src/App.js`

```jsx
import React from "react";
import LocalState from "./components/LocalState";

function App() {
  return <LocalState />;
}

export default App;
```

### `src/components/LocalState.jsx`

```jsx
import React, { useState } from "react";

function LocalState() {
  const [name, setName] = useState("");
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        placeholder="Enter name"
        value={name}
        onChange={(event) => setName(event.target.value)}
      />

      <p>Hello, {name}</p>
      <p>Count: {count}</p>

      <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
        Increase
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default LocalState;
```

## Output

```text
[Enter name]

Hello, Sanika
Count: 0

[Increase]
```

After clicking **Increase**, the count increments by 1.

## Result
Successfully managed local component state using the `useState` hook in React.
